$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Sulfamide Synthesis:
N-(2-Allyl-phenyl)-N'-benzyl-sulfamide (1a).2 A solution of
o-Allylaniline (3.00 g, 22.5 mmol) and triethylamine (4.56 g, 5.98 mL,
45.08 mmol) in dry benzene (100 mL) was cooled to 0 °C and treated with a
0.1 M solution of benzylsulfonylchloride1 in benzene (7.73 g, 37.6 mmol).
After warming to room temperature, the mixture was allowed to stir for 24
h and the solvent was removed in vacuo. Chromatograpy of the crude oil on
SiO2 (10-30% Et2O/hexanes gradient) provided 6.14 g, 90% of sulfamide 1a
as a yellow/brown solid. Data for 1a: mp = 50-52 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.50 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.29-7.11 (m, 8 H), 6.43 (s, 1 H),
5.92 (m, 1 H), 5.12 (m, 2 H), 4.67 (m, 1 H), 4.22 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 2 H),
3.37 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2 H); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3) δ 136.0, 135.6,
130.7, 130.7, 129.9, 128.8, 128.1, 127.9, 127.9, 125.2, 121.0, 117.2,
47.6, 36.5; IR (neat, thin film) 3302, 1494, 1328, 1152, 919, 751 cm-1;
HRMS (EI) calcd for [M]+ C16H18N2O2S: 302.1089, found 302.1084.
