$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Sulfonyl Azides 2a-f; General Procedure A
solution of NaN3 (195 mg, 3.00 mmol) in H2O (10 mL) was added dropwise to
a solution of the sulfonyl chloride 4a-f (3 mmol) in acetone (15 mL) and
DMF (15 mL). The reaction was stirred at r.t. for up to 1 h. After
evaporation of acetone, H2O (200 mL) was added and the product
precipitated. The mixture was filtered and the residue was washed with 5%
NaHCO3 soln (10 mL), H2O (50 mL), and dried in vacuo. Sulfonyl azides
2a-f were all obtained as white solids. 2f (Derived from
Fmoc-Ser(t-Bu)-OH)17 Scale: 1.62 mmol; yield: 0.55 g (74%). Rf = 0.73
(MeOH-CH2Cl2, 1:99); mp 103 °C. IR (KBr): 2137 (s) cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.19 [s, 9 H, C(CH3)3], 3.51, 3.64 (2 m, 4 H, CH2SO2,
t-BuOCH2), 4.23 [t, 1 H, CH (Fmoc)], 4.35- 4.51 [m, 3 H, CH2 (Fmoc),
NCH], 5.33 (br d, 1 H, NH), 7.30-7.78 [m, 8 H, Ar-CH (Fmoc)]. 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 27.4 [C(CH3)3], 47.1, 47.6 [NCH, CH (Fmoc)], 55.9
(CH2SO2), 61.7 (t-BuOCH2), 67.0 [CH2 (Fmoc)], 73.8 [C(CH3)3], 120,0,
124.9, 125.0, 127.1, 127.8, 141.3, 143.6 [Ar- C (Fmoc)], 155.5 [C=O
(Fmoc)]. ESI-MS: m/z (%) = 459 [M + H]+, 481 [M + Na]+, 497 [M + K]+, 917
[2M + H]+. Anal. Calcd for C22H26N4O5S: C, 57.63; H, 5.72; N, 12.22.
Found: C, 57.49; H, 5.66; N, 12.06.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
