$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (±)-N-Benzyl-N’-[2-(1-hydroxy-2-methyl-allyl)-phenyl]-sulfamide (9).
Aniline 22 (0.39 g, 0.0024, 1 equiv) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (10 mL).
Pyridine (0.19 ml, 0.0024, 1 equiv) and benzylaminesulfonyl chloride
(0.49g, 0.0023, 0.99 equiv) were added and the solution was stirred
overnight at 23 °C. The reaction mixture was washed with water, dried
over Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. Purification of the crude residue
by flash chromatography on SiO2 (10–20 % EtOAc / hexane as eluent)
afforded 0.42 g of sulfamide 9 (53 % yield) as a viscous, colorless oil.
Data for 9: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7. 96 (s, 1 H), 7.57 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 1 H), 7.32 (dd, J = 8.7, 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.25 (m, 2 H), 7.15-7.08 (m, 4
H), 5.27 (s, 1 H), 5.18 (s, 1 H), 5.09 (s, 1 H), 4.7 (m, 1 H), 4.20 (ddd,
J = 5.49, 5.49, 5.86 Hz, 2 H), 2.29 (s, 1 H), 1.63 (s, 3 H) 13C NMR
(75.45 MHz) δ 144.7, 136.5, 136.3, 129.3, 129.1, 128.8, 128.7, 127.9,
123.7, 119.9, 111.7, 77.4, 47.4, 19.4; IR (neat, thin film) 3500, 3305,
3075, 3028, 2922, 1587, 1496, 1448, 1418, 1329, 1150, 1061, 930 cm-1;
HRMS (ESI) calcd for [M+Na]+ C17H20N2NaO3S: 355.1087, found 355.1086.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper(II) Acetate Promoted Intramolecular Diamination of Unactivated
Olefins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zabawa, Thomas P.; Kasi, Dhanalakshmi; Chemler, Sherry R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(32), 11250-11251

