$DATUM A solution of allylamine 23 (0.1 g, 0.58 mmol, 1 equiv) and pyridine
(0.047 mL, 0.58 mmol, 1 equiv) in 3 mL of CH2Cl2 was cooled to 0 °C and
treated with a solution of benzylaminesulfonyl chloride (0.12 g, 0.57
mol, 0.99 equiv) in 5 mL of CH2Cl2. After being stirred 12 h at 23 °C ,
the crude product in CH2Cl2 was washed with water. The aqueous layer was
extracted with CH2Cl2 and the combined organic layers dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude oil was purified by flash
chromatography on SiO2 (30–40% EtOAc/hexane eluent), providing 0.1 g of
sulfamide (53% yield) as a white solid. Data for 13: mp 68-69 °C; 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.41-7.39 (m, 1 H), 7.29 -7.23 (m, 6 H), 6.97 (m, 2
H), 5.9 (m, 1 H), 5.73 (m, 1 H), 5.23-5.18 (m, 2 H) 5.06 – 4.99 (m, 2 H)
4.80 (m, 1 H), 4.67 (m, 1 H), 4.01 (d, J = 12.8 Hz, 1 H), 3.91 (m, 1 H),
3.72 (d, J = 11.7 Hz, 1 H), 3.58 (dd, J = 15.7, 6.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.45 (dd, J
= 16.1, 5.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.55-2.40 (m, 2 H); 13C NMR (75.5 MHz) δ 139.6,
137.2, 136.9, 136.1, 133.4, 130.3, 128.5, 128.0, 127.8, 127.7, 126.9,
126.3, 119.5, 116.2, 52.3, 47.1, 41.7, 36.9; IR (neat, thin film) 3283,
1426, 1313, 1151, 1061 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for [M+Na]+ C20H24N2NaO2S:
379.1451, found 379.1447.
