$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N -Benzyl-N’-(2-methyl-allyl-phenyl)-sulfamide (7). A solution of
2-Aminobenzylalcohol (3.86 g, 0.031 mol, 1 equiv) and pyridine (3 mL,
0.038 mol, 1.2 equiv) in 100 mL of CH2Cl2 was cooled to 0 °C and treated
with benzylaminesulfonyl chloride (6.4 g, 0.031 mol, 0.99 equiv) in 20 mL
of CH2Cl2. After being stirred 12 h at 23 °C, the volatiles were removed
in vacuo. The crude product was dissolved in EtOAc (100 mL) and washed
with saturated aqueous (20 mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with
EtOAc (2x100 mL) and the combined organic layers dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude oil was purified by flash
chromatography on SiO2 (30–40% EtOAc/hexane eluent), providing 3.9 g of
sulfamide 20 as a white solid (43% yield). Data for (2-sulfamido
benzylalcohol 20): mp 79-81 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.86 (s, 1 H),
7.55 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.33 (dd, J = 7.6, 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.25 (m, 3
H), 7.16 (m, 2 H), 7.08 (t, J = 7.3, Hz, 1 H), 4.83 (s, 1 H), 4.66 (s, 2
H), 4.25 (d, J = 5.8 Hz, 2 H), 1.95 (bs, 1 H); 13C NMR (75.45 MHz) δ
136.9, 136.2, 129.3, 129.2, 128.9, 128.6, 127.89, 127.86, 124.2, 120.3,
64.0, 47.4; IR (neat, thin film) 3307, 3056, 2926, 1603, 1589, 1497,
1455, 1418, 1330, 1265, 1153, 1060, 1003, 934 cm-1; HRMS (EI) calcd for
[M]+ C14H16N2O3S1: 292.0876, found 292.08646.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper(II) Acetate Promoted Intramolecular Diamination of Unactivated
Olefins
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zabawa, Thomas P.; Kasi, Dhanalakshmi; Chemler, Sherry R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(32), 11250-11251

